{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1785088828,"nonce":"ffDI+5F7qJO3tzRLrHZN11eQGbE=","title":"Scarab-shipped node driver, part of the standard install (incl. kind/colima).","message":"Mounts a Workspace Snapshot as a read-only lower layer with a pod-local\nwritable upper layer.\n\nLazy materialisation is the point: a Step transfers what it READS, not what\nit inherits. This is what makes wide edges affordable without authors\ndeclaring anything (ADR-0061's governing principle) — and it is the only\nmechanism that can, since intercepting reads needs a privileged mount an\nunprivileged Pod cannot arrange.\n\nService (s1) + driver are one component in two halves.\n\nDepends on: s1.","files":null}]}